-- title:
--   Inertia order equals ramification index for a discrete place
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field and $G$ a finite group acting faithfully on $F$ by ring automorphisms, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $F$ whose underlying ring is a discrete valuation ring. Write $R := P \cap F^G$ for the comap of $P$ along the inclusion of the fixed subfield $F^G$ into $F$, and assume the residue field of the local ring $R$ is perfect. Let $\varphi : R \to P$ be the ring homomorphism sending an element of $F^G$ lying in $P$ to the same element viewed in $P$. Then the ideal of $P$ generated by the image under $\varphi$ of the maximal ideal of $R$ equals the maximal ideal of $P$ raised to the power $N$, where $N$ is the cardinality of the set of those $g \in G$ which satisfy $g \cdot P = P$ and $g \cdot e - e \in \mathrm{nonunits}(P)$ for every $e \in P$, i.e. which fix $P$ and act trivially on $P$ modulo its maximal ideal. Thus the order of the inertia group of $P$ in $G$ is the ramification index $e(P \mid P \cap F^G)$.
--
--   This is Hilbert's ramification theory for the Galois extension $F/F^G$, in the shape $\mathfrak m_R P = \mathfrak m_P^{|I_P|}$: the inertia group of a discrete place is exactly as large as the ramification index, under the hypothesis that the residue field below is perfect. It is used for computations of place widths on modular curves with the diamond operators acting, and in a variant statement identifying the same power from a hypothesis on the order of a group of automorphisms fixing the place.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_map_maximalIdeal_comap_fixedPoints_eq_maximalIdeal_pow_card_inertia.lean

